// A note below the tab's lowest string can't be fretted; rather than clamp it to
// a wrong open string (fret 0), the tab shows NOTHING for it — no fret number, no
// stem, and a fully out-of-range beam group drops its beam too. The notation staff
// still shows every note at its true pitch. Measure 1 is in range; measure 2 sits
// an octave below the bass's low E, so its whole (beamed) run is blank on the tab.
title "Tab below range"
time 4/4
key c major

part m {
  instrument bass
  section A { e8 f g a e f g a | c,8 d, e, f, c, d, e, f, | }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  staff m
  tab m
}
